[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known, with one fix queued. Its reports describe two bugs.
That one fix leaves the second bug in place.

## What the reports show

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table runs `causes.ts` over the export, after dropping the copies of a report that overlapping
export pages create. The last column compares each cause with #4471. The hint bug now has its own
ticket, listed below.

## The two bugs

- **`parser`:** the shared parser reads every date month first, so a day-first tenant's dates come
  out flipped. This is the bug #4471 names.
- **`hint`:** `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people type month first, and
  the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. This happens only on the `form` channel, for
  tenants on `booking-v3`.

A parser fix changes how the shared parser reads dates. It does not change what `booking-v3` prints,
so people on that form still type the month first.

## Tickets

Ticket links follow once the tickets are filed.

## Why one ticket hid this

<Callout kind="warn">
Report text and intake tags cannot separate these bugs. Both bugs produce the same complaint, and
intake tags come from the reporter's browser. Only the tenant and the channel separate them.
</Callout>

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone, so nobody had to read
or look up anything. The decision stays as accepted; changing the rule takes a new record.

## What we do not know

The one-day reports in the table's note do not read like a flip. One describes clients in Lisbon and
Toronto getting different days, which suggests a time zone. They stay under the cause of their
tenant and channel, as the desk filed them. Nothing in the export shows what caused them, so check
them again once the parser fix ships.

